course: dictionary
lesson: 5117
title: One word, four meanings: introduce
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word introduce has more than one meaning, so the sentence around it tells you which meaning is right. «Grandma, this is Tom.» Here, introduce means telling two people each other's names when they meet for the first time.
explain: Look at what happens next to decide. «A new pet should be introduced slowly, with an adult watching.» A pet is not being given a name here. It is being brought into a home for the first time, carefully, so introduce means bring in or start using something new.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If «introduce» means start for the first time, does «A new pet should be started slowly» still make sense? It does, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: Introduce means to tell people each other's names when they meet for the first time.
fact: Introduce also means to bring in or start using something new, such as a new rule.
fact: «Introduction» is the word for the first part of a talk, book or piece of writing, which tells you what is coming.
fact: «Introduce yourself» means to say your own name to someone you have not met before.
exercise: «A new pet should be introduced slowly, with an adult watching.» What does introduced mean here? | Counted out loud | *Brought in slowly and carefully for the first time | Thrown out quickly | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «When someone introduces themselves, you answer, "Nice to meet you."» What does introduces themselves mean? | Writes you a long letter | Hides their name from you | Runs away quickly | *Tells you their name when meeting you
exercise: «The first paragraph introduces what is coming.» What does introduces mean here? | Breaks into small pieces | *Tells the reader what is coming | Forgets the story | Makes the story longer
test: «The teacher will introduce a new rule on Monday.» What does introduce mean here? | Ask everyone to leave | Forget the rule | Hide the rule in a drawer | *Start using the rule for the first time
test: Ella wants to tell a new classmate her name. Which phrase fits? | *Introduce yourself | Forget yourself | Carry yourself | Hide yourself
exam: «Rabbits were introduced to Australia, and this caused harm to the land.» What does introduced mean here? | Taught to read | Sent back home quickly | Eaten by the local animals | *Brought to a new place for the first time
